WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.959
(slow piano music)

00:00:01.959 --> 00:00:05.048
- [Narrator] This is Goliath,
a Galapagos tortoise.

00:00:05.048 --> 00:00:06.215
He is massive.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.674
At over 520 pounds,

00:00:11.674 --> 00:00:14.556
he's one of the biggest
tortoises in the world.

00:00:14.556 --> 00:00:17.308
Goliath is believed to be in his 80s.

00:00:17.308 --> 00:00:21.475
Galapagos tortoises have been
known to live over 150 years.

00:00:22.451 --> 00:00:24.018
They can go extended periods of time

00:00:24.018 --> 00:00:27.768
without food or water, up to a year.

00:00:27.768 --> 00:00:30.555
This unfortunately led
to human exploitation.

00:00:30.555 --> 00:00:32.728
Sailors on ships would
bring these slow moving

00:00:32.728 --> 00:00:36.895
defenseless giants on long
voyages as a source of meat.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.269
By the 1970s, only about 3,000 were left,

00:00:42.269 --> 00:00:44.603
but through conservation
and breeding efforts,

00:00:44.603 --> 00:00:46.770
there are now over 20,000.

00:00:48.016 --> 00:00:49.618
They've become a flagship species

00:00:49.618 --> 00:00:52.764
for conservation efforts
throughout the Galapagos.

00:00:52.764 --> 00:00:57.283
But poaching and habitat loss
are still a very real threat.

00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:59.472
This is the Galapagos tortoise.

00:00:59.472 --> 00:01:02.389
(slow piano music)

